# Build products of the experiments: binaries, object files, synthetic root
# filesystems and raw strace logs. These are REGENERATED by re-running the
# numbered script, which is the reproduction path the methodology asks for.
#
# ⚠ THE DISTINCTION THAT MATTERS. docs/methodology/experiments.md says an
# experiment "does not clean up its own output ... the evidence is the point".
# The evidence kept here is the SCRIPT plus the RESULT it printed, both
# tracked. What is ignored is the multi-megabyte intermediate a re-run
# recreates byte for byte. A result that cannot be regenerated by re-running
# the script does not belong under evidence/ at all -- it belongs in docs/.
evidence/*/build/
evidence/*/*.trace

# Root filesystems live outside the tree by default ($PGB_ROOTFS_DIR), but a
# caller can point --dest here.
/rootfs/

# Tool build output
/tool/target/
*.o
*.so.tmp
